{"rule": "Return this JSON object with the rule field unchanged and a new passage of about 250 words in the text field.", "text": "By the end of the month the bud had opened into three leaves, each no larger than a fingernail, and the girl began visiting the hollow before school as well as after. Her father came too, though he pretended otherwise. He would appear at the edge of the heather with a bucket of seaweed from the shore, saying he had meant to spread it on the potatoes and had simply taken the long way round. She let him keep the pretense. Together they worked the seaweed into the soil in a ring around the stake, careful not to disturb the roots. One grey morning he brought a length of old fishing net and showed her how to stretch it over a frame of driftwood so the wind would break against it before reaching the tree. 'Your mother tried this,' he said, 'but she set it too close. The net rubbed the bark raw.' He moved the frame back a full stride and hammered the posts in with the flat of a stone. The girl watched his hands, broad and cracked from the winter, and thought of her mother's hands doing the same work, alone, year after year. In May a storm came in off the Atlantic and blew for two days. She lay awake listening to the shutters rattle, certain the tree was gone. At first light she ran to the hollow. The net had torn loose on one side and flapped like a sail, but behind it the three leaves had become five. Her father arrived a minute later, breathing hard, still in his slippers."}
